cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TTB1 (v0.2.0 / TTB2) in your research or software, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "TTB1: Cycloidal Hub-Entangled Succinct Ternary Serialization and SIMD/OpenMP Execution Engine"
version: 0.2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24379185
date-released: 2026-11-20
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DRL-233/TTB1-Succinct-Threaded-Ternary-Binary-Serialization-and-SIMD-OpenMP-Execution-Engine"
abstract: >
  TTB1 (v0.2.0 / TTB2 wire protocol) is a succinct binary wire format (~2.60-2.84 bits/node)
  and load-time basic-block fusion runtime for cycloidal hub-entangled ternary trees.
  By combining 5-trit degree packing, predicate-sparse threaded cross-links,
  hemispherical geodesic spoke addressing (2*pi*R^2) for O(1) center-to-periphery
  flight and dynamic sibling jumps, and 64-byte aligned zero-copy payloads, TTB1
  achieves up to 30.8x wire compression and >1,325x faster tree execution than
  standard JSON pipelines without floating-point or matrix operations.
keywords:
  - succinct data structures
  - ternary tree
  - cycloidal hub-and-spoke addressing
  - bytecode compiler
  - basic block fusion
  - SIMD
  - OpenMP
  - zero-copy serialization
  - edge computing
authors:
  - family-names: "Asare-Darko"
    given-names: "Matthias"
